  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "It is important to be aware of the warning signs of sexually transmitted infections (STIs) and to seek medical attention if you suspect you may have been exposed to an STI. Some common warning signs of STIs include:\n\n  1. Unexplained fever, chills, or fatigue\n  2. Unusual discharge or bleeding from the vagina or penis\n  3. Painful urination or sexual intercourse\n  4. Sores, blisters, or rashes on the genitals or anus\n  5. Nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea\n  6. Swollen lymph nodes in the groin or neck\n\nIf you experience any of these warning signs, it is important to seek medical attention as soon as possible. It is also important to be honest with your healthcare provider about your sexual history and any symptoms you may be experiencing. This information can help your healthcare provider make an accurate diagnosis and recommend appropriate treatment.",
